From: HSL maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] hdmi: use available DRM types independently of the KMS backend

The Wayland backend includes drm_include.h even when HAVE_DRM=0. That
header already imports drm_mode.h, so declaring fallback HDR structures
again breaks nested-only builds. Header availability does not enable the
DRM backend, device access, or any runtime graphics feature.

Keep the fallback for targets without the standard DRM header.

--- a/src/hdmi.h
+++ b/src/hdmi.h
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@
 #define HDMI_EOTF_ST2084 2
 #define HDMI_EOTF_HLG 3
 
-#if HAVE_DRM
+#if HAVE_DRM || __has_include(<drm_mode.h>)
 #include <drm_mode.h>
 #else
 /**
